From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree: ICorDebug breakpoints and stepping over Wine Mono's
 debugger agent

NET-DBG phase 2, third part (wine-sg 7797). Breakpoints and steppers are
the agent's event requests, their hits ICorDebugManagedCallback events:
- ICorDebugFunction::CreateBreakpoint and GetILCode, ICorDebugCode
  (IsIL, GetFunction, CreateBreakpoint at an IL offset): an
  ICorDebugFunctionBreakpoint is a BREAKPOINT request (LOCATION_ONLY at
  method and offset, suspend all), active when made, Activate(FALSE)
  clears it.
- ICorDebugThread::CreateStepper: Step (into or over), StepRange (the
  same: the agent steps by sequence points), StepOut; a STEP request on
  the thread, cleared once it completes or on Deactivate.
- The agent's composite events, from the connection's reader thread, are
  queued and delivered by a thread of the process: Breakpoint and
  StepComplete with the thread and a minimal ICorDebugAppDomain (the
  default domain), the process stopped (as after Stop) until continued.
  An event whose breakpoint or stepper is gone resumes the program.
